    "explanation": "This ruling decides the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee charged on trip TRP-00406. The fee stands, and the driver is paid SGD 3.20.\n\nWHY THE FEE STANDS. POL-NS-01 makes a no-show fee chargeable only where four conditions all hold, and they do. (a) The trip record (EV-TRIP-00406) carries a driver 'arrived' event at 09:10:45. (b) The driver's own device trace (EV-GPS-00406) places him inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius from 09:10:45 — 33 consecutive qualifying fixes under the 25 m accuracy filter, the closest 4.25 m from the pin. (c) He held position inside that geofence for 320 continuous seconds, from 09:10:45 to the cancellation at 09:16:05, against the 300-second free waiting period in force on the trip record (platform_policy.free_wait_sec, 300 s) — a surplus of 20 seconds. (d) No boarding event is recorded and the trip was terminated by the driver at 09:16:05 under RIDER_NO_SHOW, one of the three reason codes limb (d) recognises, at or after the moment the 300 seconds elapsed at 09:15:45. The arrival marker is the driver's own button, not a GPS_AUTO arrival, so POL-NS-12 assists neither party — but the arrival and the dwell are established on the exported trace itself (100 per cent coverage, 64 fixes, no gap, single 33-fix run), which is the strict reading the rider asks for. POL-NS-06 does not apply: the derived shortfall is minus 20 seconds, i.e., a surplus. POL-NS-03 does not apply: it governs drivers stationary outside the arrival radius but within 400 m of the pin, and the driver's fixes here are inside the radius. The ledger's cancellation-fee line of SGD 4.00 reconciles with platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd of SGD 4.00, so there is no POL-NS-08(d) fare defect and no mis-selected reason code to refer.\n\nTO THE RIDER. I accept both of your factual points. Your message at 09:11:40 ('im at blk 12 void deck, cant see any car, where r u?') is a properly locating message, and your own track (EV-GPS-00406 rider_presence) puts your device stationary within 45 m of the pin for the whole window. Neither of those refunds the fee. The clause that converts a present, coordinating rider into a refund is POL-NS-04, and it fails its limb (b): that limb requires the driver neither to have replied in chat within 120 seconds nor to have placed an in-app call before terminating. He placed an in-app call at 09:12:15, 35 seconds after your message — 18 seconds, unanswered, recorded on the trip record (in_app_calls). The clause is drafted so that a call answers it whether or not it is picked up, and that is why your presence and your message, though true, do not exonerate you. Your argument that RIDER_NO_SHOW is the driver's 'unverified inference' does not defeat limb (d): the clause reads the recorded cancellation reason code as its own test, the code is one of the three it recognises, and it was set after the waiting period had run.\n\nON YOUR ESCALATION ARGUMENT (POL-NS-09(b)). You ask for a holding — a direct conflict between admissible artifacts on arrival, dwell or rider presence that no clause resolves. There is none. The trip record and the trace agree on arrival and on dwell. The RIDER_NO_SHOW value is a reason the driver recorded, not a measurement of where you were, and POL-NS-01(d) takes that recorded code as its test; it is satisfied. The question your presence raises — whether POL-NS-04 exonerates you — is answered by that clause, and answered no, because of the call. A conflict the policy's own clause resolves is not the unresolved conflict POL-NS-09(b) describes, so the fee is not held and I do not escalate. Your related point that NO_ACTION leaves the SGD 4.00 charge in place while escalation would hold it is correct as far as it goes, but it only matters if the case is genuinely unresolved, and it is not.\n\nTO THE DRIVER. Your account — that you called when you saw the message and waited the full time — is consistent with the chat log (EV-CHAT-00406: your call at 09:12:15, cancellation at 09:16:05) and with the trace. Under POL-NS-07 you are paid 80 per cent of the SGD 4.00 fee, SGD 3.20, the net figure the ledger itself computes (EV-FARE-00406, driver_compensation 3.20), the residual SGD 0.20 being retained as the platform service fee. The anti-farming check does not withhold it: your no_show_terminations_30d is 1, below the 4 the clause requires, and 1 divided by 120 completed trips in 30 days is 0.008, below the 0.08 rate; both limbs must hold, and neither does (EV-DPROF-00406). Because compensation is paid, the ruling value is DRIVER_COMPENSATION and amount_sgd mirrors driver_compensation_sgd at SGD 3.20; the rider's charge stands as recorded.\n\nWEIGHT AND CONFIDENCE. Every artifact carrying a deciding fact — the trip record, the GPS trace, the fare ledger and the chat log — is COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0 with no issue codes, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00406-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0, but nothing rests on it: POL-NS-06 limb (i) accumulation is unavailable and unnecessary because there is no shortfall. No artifact below weight 1.0 carries any finding. Confidence is 0.95. The monetary effect, SGD 3.20, is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold in POL-GEN-05, so the ruling executes on issue, subject to appeal under POL-GEN-04."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

