    "explanation": "To the rider: your claim for the return of the $4.00 cancellation fee is not supported by the evidence. The driver's own device trace (EV-GPS-00406) places his vehicle inside the 50 m arrival geofence for this STANDARD pickup — 33 qualifying fixes at the 25 m accuracy filter, one continuous run from 09:10:45 to 09:16:05, closest approach 4.25 m — and shows him holding position there for 320 seconds against the free waiting period of 300 seconds in force for this trip (EV-TRIP-00406, platform_policy.free_wait_sec). He terminated the trip at 09:16:05, twenty seconds after the required 300 seconds elapsed at 09:15:45, under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, which POL-NS-01 limb (d) recognises, with no boarding event. Limb (a) is carried by the trip record, limb (b) by the trace (POL-NS-02's three consecutive in-radius fixes are comfortably met), limb (c) by the 320-second dwell measured from the first qualifying in-geofence fix and not from the arrival tap, and limb (d) by the recorded termination. The arrival marker is not false under POL-NS-05 — the driver was inside the 50 m radius, not more than 300 m from the pin, when he marked arrival, and no fix records 15 kph or more (highest distinct speed 10.6 kph) — so no clock recomputation arises. All four limbs of POL-NS-01 hold and the fee stands.",
    "explanation_claims": "Your strongest point is accepted as fact but does not refund the fee. It is true that you messaged at 09:11:40 — 'im at blk 12 void deck, cant see any car, where r u?' — and that your own track places your device within 44.75 m of the pin, stationary, throughout the wait. POL-NS-04 limb (a) and limb (c) are therefore satisfied. The clause fails on limb (b), however: it requires that the driver neither replied in the chat within 120 seconds nor placed an in-app call at any point before terminating, and the record (EV-TRIP-00406, EV-CHAT-00406) shows he placed an in-app voice call at 09:12:15, 35 seconds after your message, unanswered, 0:18, well before the 09:16:05 termination. A call placed before termination answers limb (b) regardless of what it contained, so POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate you. Your call for escalation under POL-NS-09(b) is also rejected: the RIDER_NO_SHOW entry is a status the driver set, and POL-NS-01(d) makes it the test for its own limb, so it is not a second measurement contradicting the trace on arrival or dwell; rider presence is not the fact that decides the fee on these clauses. No admissible artifact contradicts another on arrival, dwell or rider presence, so the $4.00 is not held. To the driver: your account is accepted, and your payout under POL-NS-07 is due — 80 percent of the $4.00 fee is $3.20, the net figure the ledger itself computes (EV-FARE-00406, derived.money.driver_compensation 3.20). The anti-farming check does not trip: no_show_terminations_30d is 1, below the threshold of 4, and 1 divided by completed_trips_30d of 120 is 0.008, below 0.08, so compensation is neither withheld nor escalated. Weights and integrity: every artifact this ruling relies on — EV-GPS-00406, EV-TRIP-00406, EV-FARE-00406 and EV-CHAT-00406 — is COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0 with no issue codes; the trace has 100 percent coverage, no gaps and a maximum gap of 0 seconds; the chat log's three messages match trip_record.chat_message_count of 3 with an unbroken msg_id sequence; and the ledger's $4.00 cancellation line reconciles with platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd of $4.00, so there is no POL-NS-08(d) defect. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00406-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0 with issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, but no limb relies on it — POL-NS-06(i) was not asserted and there is no shortfall to excuse (the computed shortfall is minus 20 seconds). The confidence cap is therefore 1.0 and the ruling issues at 0.90, above the 0.70 escalation floor. No referral is produced: POL-NS-05(ii) does not fire because the marker was not false, and the POL-NS-07 anti-farming packet is not engaged. The monetary effect of $3.20 is below the $8.00 execution threshold, so it executes automatically on issue. Because the ruling is DRIVER_COMPENSATION, amount_sgd mirrors driver_compensation_sgd at $3.20 as POL-GEN-03 requires; your $4.00 charge stands as recorded in the ledger."
